# Thrift Hand-Written Layer (Layer A for Thrift)

Applies to IDL, generation CMake, and wrappers — **not** to `thriftgen-*` / `gen-*` (see `thrift-generated-layer.mdc`).

## Layout

| Path | Role |
|------|------|
| `src/thrift/swcdb/Service.thrift` | Types + `Service` RPC API |
| `src/thrift/swcdb/Broker.thrift` | Empty `Broker extends Service` for C++ server stubs |
| `src/thrift/swcdb/CMakeLists.txt` | Generate into `thriftgen-${THRIFT_VERSION}`, copy to consumer `gen-*` |
| `thrift/broker/AppHandler.h` | Implements `BrokerIf` — server RPC logic |
| `thrift/broker/AppContext.h` | Handler factory + includes generated `Broker.cpp` when needed |
| `thrift/utils/Converter.h` | Thrift ↔ `SWC::DB` conversions |
| `thrift/client/Client.h` | Wraps generated `Service` client |

## Rules

- Follow normal C++ conventions (copyright, guards, `Ptr`, `SWC_LOG` / errors) on wrapper code
- Keep Thrift↔DB mapping in `Converter`; keep RPC orchestration in `AppHandler`
- Prefer splitting oversized wrappers when touching them (`AppHandler.h` is a known god file)
- Including generated `.h` / `.cpp` from wrappers is an **intentional** A↔B boundary — do not “fix” the generated targets
- Binding clients (Java/Python/Ruby/C) wrap generated `Service.Client`; keep wrappers hand-written and copyrighted

## Review

Use the **Layer A** checklist in `.cursor/rules/review-standards-clarity.mdc` (full report: `evals/STANDARDS_CLARITY_EVALUATION.md`).
